## What I changed

In `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the controller handling `POST /api/owners`), within the existing email-validation block:

1. Added a disposable-domain blocklist constant:
```java
private static final java.util.Set<String> DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS =
    java.util.Set.of("mailinator.com", "tempmail.com", "guerrillamail.com");
```

2. After the syntactic email check, extracted the domain (case-insensitively) and reject with `400 BAD_REQUEST` when it's on the blocklist:
```java
String domain = email.substring(email.indexOf('@') + 1).toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
if (DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS.contains(domain)) {
    return new ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.BAD_REQUEST);
}
```

The check sits after the `EMAIL_PATTERN` validation (so the domain is well-formed) and before the email is stored. It fits the controller's existing validate-and-return-400 idiom used for telephone, postcode, and email syntax.

